# 2-Axis Next-Generation Code Review — L0 `openOODA-core`, L1 `openOODA-kernel`, L2 `openOODA-OS`

**Date:** 2026-11-05 (first pass `07:35 HST`, second pass `18:20 HST`)
**Reviewer:** `mcode-review 1` (Stage 1 Code Reviewer, MiniMax Code)
**Scope:** 44 git repositories — L0 `openOODA-core` (10 repos), L1 `openOODA-kernel` (16 repos), L2 `openOODA-OS` (18 repos)
**Method:** Pull from the remote Forgejo host (`http://<remote-git-host>:3000`) → two-axis review → fix defects → `make verify`
+ `make test` → commit → push `origin`

---

## 0. Summary

Table columns: Axis | L0 core | L1 kernel | L2 OS
- **Standards** (Power-of-2 Shape Ladder) | **FAIL** — `BIGFILE=0`, but `MANYFN=957`, `LONGFN=336`, `DENSE=5394`; 153
  directories hold more than 8 `.oo` pages | **PASS** — 406 pages, 0 violations | **PASS** — 556 pages, 0 violations
- **Spec** (canonical imports, no toy clones, real I/O) | **PARTIAL** — the `std-hw/` resolver gap is fixed, but
  `std/sec/speculate.oo` shipped a build-breaking arena call and `std/sec/pqc.oo` has no L1 importer | **FAIL** — 10 of 16 repos
  still ship the banned `wire.oo` / `warrant.oo` / `attest.oo` / `quorum/blackbox.oo` clone set, 30 of them toy `% 1000000007`
  MACs | **PASS** — real `FsReadCap` I/O in 18 of 18; real socket I/O in the 3 network-owning daemons

Seven defects were fixed, verified, committed, and pushed. Six further findings are reported with a remediation direction. Four
findings — three from the first pass and one found in this pass — were resolved upstream while the review was running.

**Final verification state: L1 16 of 16 and L2 18 of 18 green on both `make verify` and `make test`; L0 `cli` green, `tui` and
`mcp` red only on a load artefact that reproduces identically at HEAD.**

**The second pass found the defect that matters most.** `std/sec/speculate.oo` called `oo_arena_mark()` and
`oo_arena_reset_mark(mark)`, two symbols that exist nowhere in the tree. Every consumer of the canonical `std/core/ooda.oo`
therefore failed to compile. The six L1 repositories that consume it — `oodrv-net`, `oodrv-nvme`, `oodrv-virtio`,
`ookernel-boot`, `ookernel-hal-x86`, `ookernel-sched` — were all unbuildable, and all six are green again after the repair.

---

## 1. Standards Axis — Power-of-2 Shape Ladder

### 1.1 `lint-oo-size` per layer

`/home/ubermetroid/.local/bin/lint-oo-size`, thresholds `lines>256 fns>8 longest>64 dir_files>8`:

| Layer | Root | Pages scanned | BIGFILE | MANYFN | LONGFN | DENSE | Files affected |
| :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| L0 | `/Projects/openOODA-core` | 6743 | 0 | 957 | 336 | 5394 | 5569 |
| L1 | `/Projects/openOODA-kernel` | 406 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| L2 | `/Projects/openOODA-OS` | 556 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |

`BIGFILE` is 0 in every layer, so the 256-line page ceiling holds everywhere. L1 and L2 hold all nine rungs.

### 1.2 L0 violations by repo, and the missing gate

| L0 repo | Pages | BIGFILE | MANYFN | LONGFN | DENSE | Files affected | Directories with more than 8 pages |
| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| `std` | 5374 | 0 | 898 | 240 | 4635 | 4775 | 116 |
| `oodac` | 536 | 0 | 37 | 66 | 489 | 489 | 23 |
| `tui` | 282 | 0 | 0 | 25 | 206 | 219 | 10 |
| `mcp` | 139 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| `cli` | 49 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| `opm` | 118 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| `lsp` | 119 | 0 | 0 | 4 | 49 | 51 | 3 |
| `std-hw` | 59 | 0 | 22 | 0 | 15 | 34 | 1 |
| `ooda` | 28 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 0 |
| `oodar` | 39 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **6743** | **0** | **957** | **336** | **5394** | **5569** | **153** |

The directory counts were confirmed independently with `find … -printf '%h' | uniq -c | awk '$1>8'`. The per-repo `MANYFN`,
`LONGFN`, `DENSE`, and affected-file counts sum exactly to the whole-layer totals, so the debt is confined to `std`, `oodac`,
`tui`, `lsp`, and `std-hw`; `mcp`, `cli`, `opm`, `ooda`, and `oodar` are clean.

**Root cause.** The violations survive because no L0 repository runs the shape gate:

| Layer | `verify` target |
| :--- | :--- |
| L1 and L2 (34 repos, every one) | `line-cap file-law academy density vocab check shape link-law` |
| L0 `cli`, `mcp` | `line-cap file-law academy persona` |
| L0 `tui` | `line-cap file-law academy check persona` |

L0 lacks `density`, `vocab`, `shape`, and `link-law`. That is why L1 and L2 report 0 violations while L0 reports 5569 affected
pages: the L1 and L2 gates fail closed, and the L0 gates do not exist.

### 1.3 Rule 1.14 file-type law

`rules.oot` §1.14 permits `.sh` only at `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build`, `install.sh`, `*/profile.d.sh`, `tests/test_*.sh`,
`tests/*_inner.sh`, `qa/*.sh`, `scripts/repro_*.sh`, `scripts/double_run.sh`, and `bootstrap/corpus/*/diffrun.sh`.

`cli`, `mcp`, and `tui` each shipped `scripts/link_law_gate.sh`, which is outside that list, and their own `file-law` target
failed on it. Fixed — see D4.

### 1.4 Link law (Rule 1.25)

Every L1 and L2 repository runs a `link-law` gate. No symlink and no hardlink was found in any of the 44 repositories. The
`link-law` gate in `cli`, `mcp`, and `tui` still runs after the relocation, and a planted symlink still fails it.

